No FOMC decision is scheduled this week.</li><li>Fed speaker risk: Vice Chair Michelle Bowman Tue Oct 6 at 10:45 AM ET; Governor Christopher Waller Thu Oct 8 at 4:30 AM ET. Monitor remarks for policy-path or regulatory repricing.</li><li>Fed H.4.1 reserve-balance release Thu Oct 8 at 4:30 PM ET. The Federal Reserve is closed Mon Oct 12 for Columbus Day; NYSE lists no closure that day and remains on its regular session.</li><li>Energy: EIA STEO/Winter Fuels Outlook Tue Oct 6; heating-fuels update Wed Oct 7; natural-gas storage Thu Oct 8. WPSR is shifted to Thu Oct 15 by the Columbus Day schedule.</li><li>Market structure: Cboe lists expanded SPX weekly expiration Fri Oct 9. No separate dated geopolitical or policy catalyst was verified for this window; unscheduled headlines remain risk.</li></ul></section><section style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 10px\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#c8a97a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin:0 0 8px\">Omissions and Watch</div><ul style=\"margin:0;padding-left:17px;color:#e2e8f0;font-size:10px;line-height:1.5\"><li>BLS direct Oct schedule request returned HTTP 403. The official October calendar was inspectable through the official web fallback but lists Last Modified Feb 18, 2026; because its freshness is uncertain, no future BLS release is asserted. The Oct 2 Employment Situation is already past and hidden.</li><li>DOL Initial Claims is not listed as a date-specific future release on the current DOL release page; the weekly Thursday pattern was not used to infer Oct 8.</li><li>EIA WPSR schedule places the next release on Oct 15 at 12:00 PM and 2:00 PM ET due to Columbus Day, outside this Oct 5-12 window; no Oct 7 row is inferred. Natural gas storage, heating fuels, and STEO have date-specific schedules and are included.</li><li>BEA Services Supplied Through Affiliates (2024), Oct 6 at 10:00 AM, was checked and excluded as an annual structural dataset with limited immediate ES/rates sensitivity. NAR Existing-Home Sales next publishes Oct 13 at 10:00 AM, outside the window.</li><li>TreasuryDirect current auction data confirms only the Oct 5 13/26-week and Oct 6 6-week bill auctions in the window; no later offerings/cutoffs were inferred. Date/time conflict check reconciled BEA/Census trade on Oct 6 at 8:30 AM and the EIA WPSR holiday shift.</li><li>Market snapshot quotes are delayed and single-source (Yahoo Finance); the 10Y yield, SOFR and NFCI use official Treasury, NY Fed and Chicago Fed data. No missing market quote was invented.</li></ul></section><section style=\"background:#1a1f2e;border:1px solid #2d3748;border-radius:12px;padding:14px;margin:0 0 10px\"><div style=\"font-size:11px;font-weight:700;color:#c8a97a;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.6px;margin:0 0 8px\">Trading Strategy Note | ES Futures</div><div style=\"display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:8px\"><div style=\"background:rgba(52,211,153,.07);border:1px solid rgba(52,211,153,.22);border-radius:9px;padding:10px\"><div style=\"font-size:9px;color:#34d399;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px\">BASE CASE</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;color:#e2e8f0\">Moderate scheduled risk: focus on 10:00 AM ET ISM Services today; bill auctions follow. ES was modestly lower overnight while Friday yields rose 4 bp and MOVE stayed in the moderate band. Require price and rates confirmation; scenario framework, not a directional call.</div></div><div style=\"background:rgba(248,113,113,.07);border:1px solid rgba(248,113,113,.22);border-radius:9px;padding:10px\"><div style=\"font-size:9px;color:#f87171;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:4px\">INVALIDATION</div><div style=\"font-size:10px;color:#e2e8f0\">Reassess the quiet-session assumption if ES breaks and holds beyond its overnight range with confirming Treasury-yield or volatility repricing. FOMC minutes Wed 2:00 PM ET are the next policy catalyst; this is not a trade signal.</div></div></div></section>"}
